+## Ticket 1: card 33, the depth toggle on the answer's status strip
+
+Decided from the reader's chair: someone reading an answer in Plain language who wants the researcher detail should not have to retype the question. The mockups the ticket pointed at, `testing/Developer/reports/2026-09-14_handover_inputs/design/Main.dc.html` and `Researcher.dc.html`, draw exactly this: a bare two-button pill beside "Show work" in the status strip, no repeated "Answer mode" label, no repeated info button (both belong to `DepthControl`'s pre-ask placement).
+
+What I built:
+
+- `frontend/src/components/controls/DepthControl.tsx`: a new exported `DepthStripToggle`, transcribing that pill from the mockup with the same tokens `DepthControl`'s own buttons already use (`layer1Wash`, `layer1`, `inkMuted`, `line`). It reuses the same `AUDIENCE_MODE_OPTIONS` list (renamed from a private `OPTIONS` and exported) so the two controls can never offer different choices. Clicking the already-selected option is a no-op, so a stray click never burns a run.
+- `frontend/src/components/screens/AnswerScreen.tsx`: `AnswerBody` and `AnswerScreen` both gained `onDepthChange`/`depthValue` props. The trailing status-strip group (previously just "Show work") now wraps the toggle and "Show work" together under one `margin-left: auto`, matching the mockup's own grouping. The toggle is wired into the ONE `AnswerBody` call that renders the live, landed turn, never the streaming preview and never a folded previous turn's `AnswerBody`, so it structurally cannot appear while a run is in flight or on a question the reader is no longer looking at. That is the whole enforcement of item 9.12's lock: there is no separate `locked` flag threaded from `App`, because the component that would need it never mounts during a run.
+- `frontend/src/App.tsx`: `onDepthChange={(next) => void ask(searchView.question, next, true)}`. Switching depth re-runs the SAME question through the SAME `ask` a typed follow-up uses, `continuesThread=true`, so the answer just read folds into the thread instead of vanishing, exactly as "the new answer is shown the way a new run is shown today" asks. It counts as one question against the daily cap because it is, mechanically, one more call to `ask`.
+
+## Ticket 2: card 31, every count names what it counts
+
+The TP53 finding (`testing/Developer/reports/2026-09-20_tp53_findings/findings.md`, D-2) showed a status strip's "78 sources from 3 layers", a lead sentence's "of 124 available", and a table pager's "Showing 1 to 10 of 59", three honest numbers about three different things with nothing telling a reader which was which. From the reader's chair: three different numbers under one answer, with no reader-visible label distinguishing them, reads as a system that does not know its own count, not as three legitimately different facts. Fixed the two frontend-rendered ones:
+
+- `frontend/src/hooks/useRunView.ts`: the status strip's meta line now says `"N sources cited from M layers"` rather than a bare `"N sources"`. The number is unchanged; only the word naming it changed.
+- `frontend/src/components/screens/AnswerScreen.tsx`: added `recordRowNoun` and `recordsCountLabel`, which read a records block's own `label` (set by `parseRecordLine` for a `record_line` block, e.g. "Disease name") and derive a plain noun ("disease") by stripping the trailing field word. The table/stacked-list pager's status line now reads `"Showing 1–10 of 59 disease rows, 10 per page"` where a noun is derivable, or `"...of 59 records, 10 per page"` when it is not (a `table_row`/`list_item` block carries no entity name to draw from). The page-size figure is now stated, not left implicit beside "Page 1 of 6".
+- The Sources disclosure's badge (the total distinct-record count) keeps its visible bare-number glyph, per the design system's own badge shape, but now carries an accessible name saying what it counts and, deliberately, naming why it can legitimately differ from the strip's own count: it is a count of distinct records after URL deduplication, while the strip counts citation MARKERS, and one record can answer for more than one marker.
+
+Backend text is another builder's, per the ticket, and unchanged here. What I found and what I'd recommend to whoever owns it:
+
+- `src/system_03_search_agent/core/graph.py`, `_build_truncated_answer_note` (around line 7431): the exact "not shown above" wording D-3 named is ALREADY fixed. It now says "were retrieved" or "were retrieved" versus "included in this answer" depending on `retrieval_limited`, and never says "shown above" next to a pager. Nothing to do here; noting it so nobody re-opens a closed item.
+- `src/system_03_search_agent/synthesis/answer_layout.py`, lines 1056 and 1080: the lead sentence's `", out of {total} available"` and `", of {total} available"` are still bare. I'd recommend `", of {total} records that matched this question"`, echoing the truncation note's own phrasing ("records that matched this question") so the SAME number is described the SAME way everywhere it appears in one answer, rather than "available" in one sentence and "matched" in another for what is the same underlying count.
