+## Ticket 3: card 30, a CLI example that works as printed
+
+Measured: `s3 login` with no argument fails, because `main.py`'s `_parse_login_args` declares `email` a required positional with no default. From the reader's chair: someone who copies the printed example and pastes it into a terminal should not hit an error on the very first line.
+
+- `frontend/src/components/screens/InfoScreens.tsx`: `CLI_EXAMPLE` now reads:
+  ```
+  export S3_BASE_URL=<this deployment's origin>
+  s3 login you@example.org
+  s3 ask "diseases linked to BRCA1"
+  ```
+  The base-URL line matters as much as the email: `_run_login` falls back to `http://127.0.0.1:8000` when neither `--base-url` nor `S3_BASE_URL` is set, so the two-line original would have quietly pointed a reader's first login at their own laptop rather than this deployment. `s3 ask` needs no base URL of its own since it reads the one `s3 login` already stored.
+  `KGX_EXAMPLE` is unchanged, per the ticket: the command is correct as printed for someone who HAS the operator-granted graph credentials, and the fix is naming that requirement rather than removing the command. The card's `body` text now says the KGX command "needs its own read-only graph database credentials, which only the operator can grant" and "will not run for a public account", so nobody is led to a command that fails silently with no explanation.
