+## What I could not verify, and why
+
+Ticket 1 asks for a 390px overflow check, "scrollWidth minus clientWidth is zero at 390." That check needs real browser layout, which is what `frontend/e2e/*.spec.ts`'s existing `scrollWidth`/`clientWidth` arms already use (`journeys/narrow-viewports.spec.ts` and others); jsdom, which every vitest test in this repository runs under, does not implement layout at all, so a `scrollWidth` assertion inside a vitest test would read `0 - 0 = 0` regardless of whether the markup actually overflows, a check that cannot fail and therefore is not a check. My instructions were vitest only and explicitly not the Playwright suite, and `frontend/e2e/` sits outside my file fence.
+
+What I did instead, and what I'd ask a Playwright-capable runner (or the product owner, on a real phone-width window) to confirm: the trailing group (`DepthStripToggle` plus "Show work") sits inside a `Box` with `flexWrap: "wrap"`, and every button carries `whiteSpace: "nowrap"`. At 390px the group wraps onto its own line under the outcome/elapsed/meta text rather than forcing the row wider than its container, the same mechanism the existing "Show work" button and the record pager's own status row already rely on. I have not driven a real 390px viewport to confirm this, so I am reporting the structural argument rather than claiming a check I did not run.
